# Context.dev and Bright Data

Application code reads credentials from the environment only. Never hardcode, log, or commit secrets.

## Context.dev

- Env var: `CONTEXT_DEV_API_KEY`
- Wrapper module: `src/contextdev.ts`
- Official SDK: `context.dev` (`new ContextDev({ apiKey, timeout, maxRetries })`)
- SDK docs: https://docs.context.dev/sdks/typescript.md

Endpoints (method names verified in `context.dev@3`):

- Scrape markdown — `POST /web/scrape` via `client.web.scrape` — https://docs.context.dev/api-reference/web-scraping/scrape.md
- Web search — `POST /web/search` via `client.web.search` — https://docs.context.dev/api-reference/web-scraping/search.md
- Brand retrieve — `POST /brand/retrieve` via `client.brand.retrieve` — https://docs.context.dev/api-reference/brand-intelligence/brand.md

Credits come from `key_metadata.credits_consumed` or the `X-Credits-Used` response header. A 400 with `error_code` `NOT_FOUND` or `WEBSITE_NOT_FOUND` is mapped to `ContextDevNotFoundError` and is not retried.

## Bright Data

- Wrapper module: `src/brightdata.ts`
- ISP proxy env: `BRD_ISP_PROXY_HOST`, `BRD_ISP_PROXY_PORT`, `BRD_ISP_PROXY_USER`, `BRD_ISP_PROXY_PASS`
- Browser API env: `BRD_BROWSER_WS`
- `fetchViaIspProxy(url, { country, session })` uses undici `ProxyAgent`
- `withBrowser(fn)` uses Playwright `chromium.connectOverCDP`
